<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Sheikhdom of Dubai</h1><p class="st-meta">1833 CE – 1971 CE · capital Dubai</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Al Maktoum sheikhdom on Dubai Creek, which turned free trade and merchant migration into the Gulf's leading commercial hub.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1833 about 800 members of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-bu-falasah">Al Bu Falasah</a> section of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bani-yas">Bani Yas</a> left the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-abu-dhabi">Sheikhdom of Abu Dhabi</a> and settled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dubai-creek">Dubai Creek</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maktoum-bin-butti">Maktoum bin Butti</a> and Obaid bin Said. Maktoum's descendants, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-maktoum">Al Maktoum</a>, have ruled since.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Dubai joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trucial-states">Trucial States</a> system and lived from pearling, fishing and trade. Low taxes drew merchants, especially from the Persian port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bandar-lengeh">Lingeh</a> after 1902, and Dubai became the main <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entrepot">entrepot</a> of the coast. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saeed-bin-maktoum-al-maktoum">Saeed bin Maktoum</a> ruled from 1912 to 1958, facing a reform movement in 1938. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashid-bin-saeed-al-maktoum">Rashid bin Saeed Al Maktoum</a> dredged the creek and opened an airport in 1960.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Offshore oil was found in 1966 and funded further building. Rashid worked with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zayed-bin-sultan-al-nahyan">Zayed</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-abu-dhabi">Abu Dhabi</a> to form the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a>, which Dubai joined at its foundation in December 1971.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sheikhdom-of-dubai.jpg" alt="Sheikhdom of Dubai" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Dubai.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1833 CE – 1971 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dubai</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Maktoum bin Butti, Saeed bin Maktoum, Rashid bin Saeed Al Maktoum</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>United Arab Emirates</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dubai, Emirate of Dubai</dd></dl></aside></div>
